; ClickHouse endpoint for the cron-job metrics hooks (src/utils/clickhouse.php).
;
; Sections are keyed by the `clickhouse:<name>` tag the ClickHouse server
; declares as its database; this client reads [clickhouse:analytics], the
; database the simox_job_runs / simox_job_counters schema lives in.
;
; Endpoint-only: host and port of the HTTP interface. The SQL user is the
; global CLICKHOUSE_USER (default `default`, a passwordless service user
; allowlisted by the server); CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD is an optional override,
; empty by default. The security boundary is ZeroTier membership plus a
; source-IP allowlist on the server, so no credential is shipped here.
;
; This client speaks the plaintext HTTP interface (8123) — the interface a PHP
; process can reach without a native driver — over ZeroTier, whose wire
; encryption makes TLS redundant.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only and is MANUALLY MAINTAINED by the
; consumer (private data: copied into etc/ as a real file by simox's
; bin/fetch-private-data in dev, shipped into the freshly swapped etc/ by the
; framework's DEPLOY_PRIVATE_FILES — see doc/system/private-config.md). The
; committed copy is this template: placeholders only, never a real endpoint.
; An absent etc/clickhouse.ini disables metrics; it never fails a job.

[clickhouse:analytics]
host = <CH ZeroTier IP>
port = 8123
